WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 010, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.846
<v Gwen>Six years this church has stood, John, and I still look for the old one. Carted off to Leckwith and put up again.

2
00:00:21.196 --> 00:00:29.658
<v Gwen>And now the parson's land is going for a school. Signed over on New Year's Day, I heard at the post office.

3
00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:35.008
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>Mr Williams? Assistant overseer, for the poor rate. Your turn, if you please.

4
00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:44.588
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>I have you entered as occupier of glebe land in this parish. Owner: the Reverend H. H. Rickards. The rate falls on the occupier.

5
00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:54.554
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>So I farm the parson's land and pay the parish for the privilege. Write it fair, then, and I'll pay my share like everyone else.

6
00:00:54.904 --> 00:01:00.673
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>The book records who occupies and who owns, Mr Williams. That is all it records.

7
00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:06.792
<v Gwen>And when you've finished with him, Mr Overseer, I've my own small one to pay.
